{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"1ca82f23-e809-40d3-8f42-b2e8531d2a01","status":"SUCCESS","response":"Prisma ORM has been added and configured for this project.\n\n### Summary of Actions Taken\n1. **Installed Prisma ORM**:\n   - Installed the current version of `prisma` CLI and target package `@prisma/orm-postgres` with `@prisma/cli-engine` and `dotenv`.\n2. **Schema \u0026 Model Definition**:\n   - Created [`prisma/contract.prisma`](file:///tmp/h-aPr8G0/prisma/contract.prisma) modeling:\n     - `User`: unique `email`, optional `name`, and relation to `posts`.\n     - `Post`: `title`, optional `content`, `published` defaulting to `false`, and relation to `author` (`User`).\n   - Generated contract artifacts (`contract.json`, `contract.d.ts`) using `npx prisma contract emit`.\n3. **Database Migration**:\n   - Applied schema changes to the local PostgreSQL database in `.env` using `npx prisma db init`, creating the tables, constraints, and indexes.\n4. **Script Creation \u0026 Verification**:\n   - Added [`script.ts`](file:///tmp/h-aPr8G0/script.ts) to create a user with two posts and print every user with their posts using `db.orm.public.User.include('posts').all()`.\n   - Verified execution with `npx tsx script.ts`.\n5. **Documentation**:\n   - Documented the changes in [`ANSWER.md`](file:///tmp/h-aPr8G0/ANSWER.md).\n","duration_seconds":366.20109,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":359502,"output_tokens":6431,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":3605793,"total_tokens":365933}}}
